<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan textile shares up on rising prices.</title>
<headline>Taiwan textile shares up on rising prices.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's textile shares surged at mid-morning on Wednesday on rising market prices for polyester drawn texturised yarn, brokers said.</p>
<p>With 75 minutes left, textiles were up 2.07 percent while the overall index had risen only 0.73 percent.</p>
<p>Lealea Enterprise rose T$1 or 4.41 percent to T$23.7. Hong Yi Fiber surged T$1.7 or 5.92 percent to T$30.4.</p>
<p>Brokers said prices of polyester drawn texturised yarn had rebounded after months of sluggishness.</p>
</text>
